    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it's not just burnout. it's deeper. it feels like the well is dry for good this time. like the person who used to create things doesn't even exist anymore. what's the point of trying to fix something that's just... fundamentally broken and empty?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear how overwhelming and hopeless that feels right now, and it’s painful to stare at a future that seems permanently barren. When the sense of self that used to create feels gone, it can help to treat it like grief—allow yourself to mourn the loss, then start with tiny, low‑stakes experiments (a doodle, a single sentence, a short walk) just to prove the well still holds a drop of water. If those feelings of emptiness and brokenness persist, reaching out to a mental‑health professional can provide a safe space to rebuild a sense of identity and purpose. You don’t have to fix everything on your own; even small steps and compassionate support can begin to refill the well.",
